SUMMARY:Lea and Heffernan of Wheelchair Sports Camp
DESCRIPTION:Gaelynn Lea and Kalyn Rose Heffernan of Wheelchair Sports Camp will visit UNC Asheville for an afternoon talk and evening performance. \nAt 3 p.m.\, Lea and Heffernan will discuss disability culture\, access\, and activism\, sharing their experiences as artists and advocates working to make the arts more inclusive. \nAt 6 p.m.\, Wheelchair Sports Camp will take the stage for a free performance. Lea\, winner of NPR Music’s Tiny Desk Contest\, is an accomplished violinist\, songwriter\, composer\, and disability advocate who has performed around the world and composed the score for Macbeth on Broadway.  \nWheelchair Sports Camp\, led by wheelchair-using rapper Kalyn Rose Heffernan\, blends hip-hop\, humor\, and high-energy performance. The Denver-based band has expanded its work beyond music into performance art\, museums\, theater\, film\, and activism. \nBoth events are free and open to the public and will take place in the Blue Ridge Room of the Highsmith Student Union. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Accessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/gaelynn-lea-wheelchair-sports-camp/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Event-Calendar-5.png
